     <details class="fq" id="buy-what-does-it-cost-me-as-a-buyer-to-use-mykunda"><summary>What does it cost me as a buyer to use MyKunda?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Nothing. Searching, saving properties, saving searches, alerts and contacting sellers are free to buyers. We charge sellers for listing upgrades, and buyers for an Ownership Verification if they choose to order one.</p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-what-does-the-verified-title-badge-on-a-listing-mean"><summary>What does the Verified Title badge on a listing mean?</summary><div class="ans"><p>That the documents the seller supplied with that listing have been reviewed by a qualified legal professional as part of the seller's plan. It is a meaningful check on the papers, and it is not a government guarantee — it cannot reach unregistered customary interests, family claims or an occupier nobody mentioned.</p>
 <p>If you are about to pay, order your own <a href="verify.html">Ownership Verification</a>: the report is addressed to you, covers the registry, the seller's identity and — on the full check — the ground itself, and you can order it on any property in The Gambia, listed with us or not.</p></div></details>
-    <details class="fq" id="buy-what-is-the-difference-between-the-verified-badge-and-an-ownership-ver"><summary>What is the difference between the Verified badge and an Ownership Verification?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Who buys it and what it covers. The <b>badge</b> is part of a seller's listing plan, paid for by the seller, covering the documents supplied with that listing. An <b>Ownership Verification</b> is a product you commission yourself on the exact property you are about to pay for; the written report is in your name, and the full check includes a site visit. Same team, same standards, different purpose.</p></div></details>
-    <details class="fq" id="buy-what-does-an-ownership-verification-cost"><summary>What does an Ownership Verification cost?</summary><div class="ans"><p>A flat fee in dalasi, never a percentage of the price: a <b>Document Check</b> at D3,500 for a desk review of everything you have been shown, and a <b>Full Ownership Check</b> at D20,000 covering the documents, the registry and the plot itself. Travel for the site visit is quoted separately and shown before you pay, because a compound in Basse is a different journey from a plot in Bijilo.</p></div></details>
+    <details class="fq" id="buy-what-is-the-difference-between-the-verified-badge-and-an-ownership-ver"><summary>What is the difference between the Verified badge and an Ownership Verification?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Who buys it and what it covers. The <b>badge</b> is part of a seller's listing plan, paid for by the seller, covering the documents supplied with that listing. An <b>Ownership Verification</b> is a product you commission yourself on the exact property you are about to pay for; the written report is in your name, and the full check includes a site visit. Same independent specialists, same standards, different purpose.</p></div></details>
+    <details class="fq" id="buy-what-does-an-ownership-verification-cost"><summary>What does an Ownership Verification cost?</summary><div class="ans"><p>A flat fee in dalasi, never a percentage of the price: a <b>Document Check</b> at D3,500 for a desk review of everything you have been shown, and a <b>Full Ownership Check</b> at D20,000 covering the documents, the registry and the plot itself. Travel for the site visit is quoted separately and shown to you before anyone travels, because a compound in Basse is a different journey from a plot in Bijilo.</p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-how-accurate-are-the-prices-on-mykunda"><summary>How accurate are the prices on MyKunda?</summary><div class="ans"><p>As accurate as the evidence allows, and we show you the evidence. The Gambia has <b>no public register of sale prices</b>, so every figure on this site is built from <b>asking prices</b> we can verify, with the number of listings behind it printed next to it. Where an area has too little evidence for a figure of its own, it shows the rate of the surrounding band, clearly marked; where we cannot defend a number, we leave it out. <a href="how-we-measure-prices.html">How we measure prices →</a></p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-is-the-valuation-tool-based-on-actual-sales"><summary>Is the valuation tool based on actual sales?</summary><div class="ans"><p>No — it cannot be, because no sale-price register exists. It is built from what is currently for sale in the area, plus the characteristics of the property, and it is an estimate rather than a valuation. For a bank, a court, an inheritance or the tax office you need a valuer who has stood on the ground.</p></div></details>
-    <details class="fq" id="buy-which-areas-does-mykunda-cover"><summary>Which areas does MyKunda cover?</summary><div class="ans"><p>All of The Gambia. We publish 46 area pages across seven regions — Greater Banjul, Kombo Coast, Kombo Inland, North Bank, Lower River, Central River and Upper River — so Basse Santa Su, Janjanbureh and Farafenni are covered as well as Kololi and Brufut. Our price evidence is deepest on the coast, and each area page says how much evidence sits behind its figures.</p></div></details>
+    <details class="fq" id="buy-which-areas-does-mykunda-cover"><summary>Which areas does MyKunda cover?</summary><div class="ans"><p>All of The Gambia. We publish 52 area pages across seven regions — Greater Banjul, Kombo Coast, Kombo Inland, North Bank, Lower River, Central River and Upper River — so Basse Santa Su, Janjanbureh and Farafenni are covered as well as Kololi and Brufut. Our price evidence is deepest on the coast, and each area page says how much evidence sits behind its figures.</p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-what-is-a-google-plus-code-and-why-does-every-listing-have-one"><summary>What is a Google Plus Code and why does every listing have one?</summary><div class="ans"><p>It is a short location code that works where street names and house numbers do not. A <b>full ten-character</b> code identifies a spot to about 14 metres and is globally unique. The <b>short</b> form you see locally — like <code>F833+6R</code> — is not: it only resolves correctly when it is paired with a town or area, because it is decoded relative to where the reader is. So always publish or record the full code, or the short code together with its locality.</p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-how-do-i-find-the-plus-code-for-a-property"><summary>How do I find the Plus Code for a property?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Open Google Maps or plus.codes, find the spot and the code appears. On a MyKunda listing it is already there, and in our listing wizard you drag the pin on the satellite map and the code fills in.</p></div></details>
     <details class="fq" id="buy-can-i-save-searches-and-be-told-when-something-new-comes-up"><summary>Can I save searches and be told when something new comes up?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Yes. Save a search from the results page and it appears in your dashboard, where you can rename it, open it, delete it and switch its alert on or off individually. Alerts go out as a single daily digest covering all your saved searches rather than one email per search, and each shows how many properties match right now.</p></div></details>
