         <p style="margin-top:18px">Farafenni has a single priced plot listing with a known size — below our bar of 5 for an area-specific rate, and there is no neighbouring band up here to borrow from. The rate above is the provincial regional rate, and it can be wide of a specific street by a factor of two. The one listing we can price in Farafenni itself asks D93 per m² — shown as context, not as a rate. Upcountry we publish land only: there is not enough house or rental advertising in Farafenni to put a number on either, and a number we cannot defend is worse than none.</p>
         <p style="margin-top:14px">Every figure on this page is an <em>asking</em> price. No one in The Gambia publishes what property actually sells for — there is no public register of sale prices — so what a seller asks is the only thing that can be measured consistently. Sale prices are generally lower, by an amount that depends entirely on the seller.</p>
