         <p style="margin-top:18px">Ghana Town has only 1 priced plot listing with a known size, and no measured band covers it either: the bands we publish are built from listings in named places, and Ghana Town is in none of them. Rather than stretch a band over it, the rate above is <strong>Brufut’s</strong> — the nearest place we have actually measured, 7 priced plot listings, 2.1 km away. It tells you what Brufut asks. The one listing we can price in Ghana Town itself asks D2,500 per m² — one seller’s opinion of one plot, shown here as context, not as a rate. Ghana Town is also hemmed in: it cannot expand seaward, because that land is Tourism Development Area, and the families who own the land around it do not allocate more. Very little changes hands here at all.</p>
         <p style="margin-top:14px">Every figure on this page is an <em>asking</em> price. No one in The Gambia publishes what property actually sells for — there is no public register of sale prices — so what a seller asks is the only thing that can be measured consistently. Sale prices are generally lower, by an amount that depends entirely on the seller. We have no rent listing we can verify here, so we quote no rental yield for this area either — a yield built on a rent we had to guess would only look like knowledge.</p>
