 <p><strong>Currency movement.</strong> The dalasi is free-floating and it moves. The Central Bank reported in February 2026 that it had fallen 11.53% against the euro and 4.36% against the dollar over the preceding year. Between agreement and completion that is a real number on a real purchase — price the risk, or agree the price in one currency and stick to it.</p>
 <p><strong>One protection worth using.</strong> If you sign abroad, the Land (Registration of Deeds) Act gives you a <strong>twelve-month window</strong> for priority to relate back to the date of execution where the instrument was executed outside The Gambia, against seven days in Banjul and sixty days elsewhere. And the Act's definition of "instrument" extends to a contract — so a sale contract, not only a final deed, can be registered. Instalment buyers in particular should use that.</p>
 <p>Purchase money should be paid into a Gambian lawyer's client account, and you should insist on it — but be clear that no Gambian rule compels it. There is no statutory client-account or escrow requirement for agents, and no mandatory deposit protection on off-plan sales.</p>
-<div class="callout"><p><b>MyKunda tip:</b> Use the savings calculator on our <a href="sell.html">Sell page</a> to see how a flat fee compares with a percentage commission, and our <a href="verify.html">Ownership Verification</a> service to check who really owns a property before any money moves.</p></div>
