 <h2 id="qa">Questions people actually ask</h2>
 <div class="qa"><h3>Is there a transfer tax when you buy property in The Gambia?</h3><p>No Gambian statute we could find imposes a buyer-paid transfer tax. The duty on an assignment or conveyance is stamp duty at 2% of the amount, and the Stamp Act (Amendment of Schedule) Order 2019 names the assignee or transferee — the buyer — as primarily liable. The "5%" widely quoted as transfer tax is, on the published law, the seller's capital gains tax floor.</p></div>
