         <p style="margin-top:18px">Madiana has only 1 priced plot listing with a known size — below our bar of 5 for an area-specific rate. The rate above is the band rate for the inland Kombo villages between the Brikama highway and the Sukuta–Jambanjelly road: 13 priced plot listings pooled across Farato, Latriya, Mamuda and Jambanjelly. It tells you what the band asks, not what a specific street asks. The one listing we can price in Madiana itself asks D1,333 per m² — one seller’s opinion of one plot, shown here as context, not as a rate.</p>
         <p style="margin-top:14px">Every figure on this page is an <em>asking</em> price. No one in The Gambia publishes what property actually sells for — there is no public register of sale prices — so what a seller asks is the only thing that can be measured consistently. Sale prices are generally lower, by an amount that depends entirely on the seller. We have no rent listing we can verify here, so we quote no rental yield for this area either — a yield built on a rent we had to guess would only look like knowledge.</p>
