 const OVFAQ = [
-  ['Can I order this for a property that is not on MyKunda?','Yes — that is the point of it. Most checks we run are on plots and houses found through another agent, a Facebook post or a family contact. We only need to know where it is and who is selling it.'],
+  ['Can I order this for a property that is not on MyKunda?','Yes — that is the point of it. This check is built for plots and houses found through another agent, a Facebook post or a family contact. We only need to know where it is and who is selling it.'],
   ['How is this different from the Verified badge on a listing?','The badge is bought by the seller as part of their listing plan and covers the documents they supplied to us. An Ownership Verification is bought by you, goes further — registry and, on the full check, the site — and the report is addressed to you, not to the listing.'],
-  ['Who actually does the check?','MyKunda sells the service and stands behind the report; the work is done by qualified specialists. Documents are read by people who read Gambian title papers for a living, registry searches are run by an independent Gambian lawyer, and where boundaries are in doubt we bring in a surveyor. They are engaged for your check and do not have to be on our payroll — we choose them, we brief them, and if the report is wrong you come to us, not to them.'],
-  ['Why is the site visit quoted separately?','Because The Gambia is long and narrow, and honesty about that is cheaper for you than an average. A plot twenty minutes from our office and a compound six hours upcountry cost us very different amounts to reach. Rolling that into one price would mean coastal buyers subsidising upcountry trips, so instead we quote the travel for your property and show it to you before anyone travels — the fee you pay on the site is the check itself. Everything else about the check costs the same either way.'],
+  ['Who actually does the check?','MyKunda sells the service and stands behind the report; the work is done by qualified specialists. Documents are read by people who read Gambian title papers for a living, registry searches are run by an independent Gambian lawyer, and where boundaries are in doubt we tell you a surveyor is needed and quote that separately before anyone is engaged. They are engaged for your check and do not have to be on our payroll — we choose them, we brief them, and if the report is wrong you come to us, not to them.'],
+  ['Why is the site visit quoted separately?','Because The Gambia is long and narrow, and honesty about that is cheaper for you than an average. A plot on the Kombo coast and a compound six hours upcountry cost us very different amounts to reach. Rolling that into one price would mean coastal buyers subsidising upcountry trips, so instead we quote the travel for your property and show it to you before anyone travels — the fee you pay on the site is the check itself. Everything else about the check costs the same either way.'],
   ['What if you cannot run the check at all?','Then you get your fee back in full. You pay when you order, and within 1–2 working days we tell you whether we can actually do the work on that property — a plot with nothing filed anywhere, or a location we cannot reach, is a check we will not pretend to run. Nothing is deducted if we have not started.'],
   ['What if the seller refuses to hand over documents?','That is itself a finding, and we will say so in writing. Where we can, we work from what is filed at the registry rather than what the seller chooses to show. If we cannot get far enough to be useful, we refund the fee minus any cost already spent.'],
   ['Do I still need my own lawyer?','Yes. This check is designed to be handed straight to your lawyer so they start from evidence rather than from scratch. It does not replace the final title search and conveyancing at completion.'],
-  ['I am buying from abroad — does that change anything?','No, and it is when this matters most. Everything happens remotely: you send what you have, we do the work in The Gambia, and the report and call happen wherever you are. Payment works by card from outside the country.'],
+  ['I am buying from abroad — does that change anything?','No, and it is when this matters most. Everything happens remotely: you send what you have, we do the work in The Gambia, and the report and the follow-up conversation (WhatsApp or email) reach you wherever you are. Payment works by card from outside the country.'],
   ['How long does a check take?','We deliberately do not put a date on it, and we would be wary of anyone who does. Registry offices, surveyors, sellers and their families in The Gambia move at their own pace, and a check that has to wait on a third party cannot be rushed by promising you a deadline. What we do commit to: we start straight away, you can ask where it stands at any point, and if something is blocked you hear it from us rather than finding out later.'],
   ['How long is a report good for?','Treat it as a snapshot of the day we looked. Registry records change, so if months pass between the report and completion, your lawyer should re-run the search before money moves.']
 ];
